---
/**
 * מחירים — what the platform charges a seller, on one public page.
 *
 * ── Why it is public and not a panel in the dashboard (CURRENT_TASK סשן ב׳: "במיקום הנכון") ──
 * The plan is chosen at the LAST moment, not the first: a seller registers, builds a whole shop and
 * looks at it with no card, and picks a plan only when he wants it to go live
 * (`lib/store-publication.ts`). That decision puts the price in two places at once — in front of a
 * stranger deciding whether to register at all, and in front of a seller deciding which plan to
 * start. They are the same comparison, so they are the same page, and it is a public one because
 * only the public version can be indexed, linked and read before anybody has an account.
 *
 * A tier card buried in the payouts panel would have been the other choice, and it is worse twice:
 * the prospect never sees it, and the seller reads a four-way comparison in a column beside a bank
 * form. What the dashboard needs instead is a LINK here, which is what the publish card's
 * "subscription" hold gives it.
 *
 * ── Server-rendered, like every other page on this site ──
 * Nothing here needs a session — "which plan am I on" is fetched afterwards
 * (`scripts/pricing-tiers.ts`) precisely so the document itself is the same for everyone. It is
 * `prerender = false` only because every page in `src/pages` is, and the header's signed-in state
 * comes from the frontmatter (see BaseLayout).
 *
 * ── Every figure is interpolated ──
 * Fees and percentages come from `lib/pricing.ts`. Nothing on this page is a typed number, because a
 * price written in a translation and again in the code is a price that will disagree with itself —
 * and the copy a seller can hold us to is this one. The one figure that is NOT here is the
 * advertising margin (`boostFeePercent`): it moved to the boost screen on 2026-08-24, beside the
 * budget field, where it is a number the seller can act on — see the ads section below.
 */
export const prerender = false;

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PricingTiers from '../components/PricingTiers.astro';
import { getLang, getT } from '../i18n/index.js';
import { getSellerSession } from '../lib/seller-auth.js';
import { getStoresBySellerId } from '../lib/stores.js';

const lang = getLang(Astro.cookies);
const t = getT(lang);
const p = t.pricing;

const sellerId = getSellerSession(Astro.cookies);
const isLoggedIn = !!sellerId;
const hasStore = sellerId ? (await getStoresBySellerId(sellerId)).length > 0 : false;

const included = [p.included1, p.included2, p.included3, p.included4, p.included5, p.included6];

const adsPoints = [p.adsPoint1, p.adsPoint2, p.adsPoint3];
const pillars = [
  { title: p.pillar1Title, body: p.pillar1Body },
  { title: p.pillar2Title, body: p.pillar2Body },
  { title: p.pillar3Title, body: p.pillar3Body },
  { title: p.pillar4Title, body: p.pillar4Body },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={p.title}
  description={p.metaDesc}
  isLoggedIn={isLoggedIn}
  hasStore={hasStore}
  storeMode={true}
  showSearch={true}
>
  <div class="container py-8 max-w-[64rem] pricing-page">
    {/* ── The page head, and nothing else in it (2026-08-24) ──
        It was a tinted band holding the heading, the lede, a line about building before you pay and
        the register button. Two things were wrong with it. The band was the loosest element on a
        page the owner then read as *"פחות מוצלח ממה שהיה, קודם היה יותר מסודר"*; and the line it
        carried told a seller he does not have to pay yet, on the one screen whose whole job is to
        get him to press a plan — *"צריך לגרום למוכר כן ללחוץ על מסלול, לא להדגיש לו שהוא לא צריך
        לשלם כרגע"*. Building before paying is still true and still the model
        (`lib/store-publication.ts`); it belongs where a seller meets it, not above the prices.
        The heading is "מסלולים" and not "מה זה עולה" for the same reason: the page offers something,
        it does not apologise for a price. */}
    <header class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-3">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-bold m-0">{p.heading}</h1>
        <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-[0.95rem] max-w-[42rem]">{p.lede}</p>
      </div>
      {!isLoggedIn && <a href="/seller/register" class="btn btn--accent">{p.ctaButton}</a>}
    </header>

    {/* ── What this is, in four cards ──
        Owner: *"הדף הזה גם נראה כאילו זה מערכת לחנויות רגילה"* — everything already connected, the
        exposure of sitting inside a marketplace, the offer to a seller who already has a shop, and
        the one he could not phrase: that the system keeps improving and every shop gets that. Four
        sentences rather than a feature list, because a feature list is what a shop builder
        publishes and this page's job is to not read like one.
        **In cards, because bare columns were read as loose** (*"יש יותר מדי אינפורמציה פזורה בלי
        שום בורדר"*). The site's own answer to a group of facts is a bordered surface each — the
        border rule was tested against a borderless version and kept for exactly this
        (memory `project_border_rule_tested_kept`). Each line names only what works today, which is
        why invoicing is absent and the stock connection is described as the hourly pull it is,
        never as two-way. */}
    <section class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 mt-6" aria-label={p.pillar1Title}>
      {pillars.map(({ title, body }) => (
        <div class="card card--flat p-4 pricing-pillar">
          <h2 class="font-semibold m-0">{title}</h2>
          <p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.88rem]">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <PricingTiers p={p} lang={lang} isLoggedIn={isLoggedIn} />

    <section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="included-title">
      <h2 id="included-title" class="text-[1.05rem] font-bold m-0">{p.includedTitle}</h2>
      {/* One list for all four plans, which is the point being made: there is nothing here that a
          tier unlocks. Ticks per column would say the opposite of the sentence at the top. */}
      <ul role="list" class="list-none p-0 m-0 mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {included.map((line) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[0.92rem]">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 mt-[0.15rem] [color:var(--color-success)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M4 10.5 8 14.5 16 6" />
            </svg>
            <span>{line}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      {/* The build-before-you-pay model, in one line, at the bottom of the list of what a plan
          includes — which is exactly where a reader is asking "and what does it cost me to find
          out". It is the platform's whole acquisition bet (`lib/store-publication.ts`), and until
          now it was stated nowhere on the page that sells the plan. Deliberately not in the head:
          the owner had that band removed on 2026-08-24 because telling a seller he does not have to
          pay yet, above the prices, is the wrong thing to lead with — *"צריך לגרום למוכר כן ללחוץ
          על מסלול"*. Under the list of what he gets, it is reassurance rather than a discount. */}
      <p class="m-0 mt-3 text-[0.88rem]">{p.includedFree}</p>
    </section>

    {/* ── Advertising: a capability, not a fee schedule (2026-08-24) ──
        This section used to be one muted sentence that opened on "בתוספת דמי ניהול של X%", and the
        owner's reading of it was that the page mentions the tool only in order to charge for it —
        *"חסר שם מידע על זה שיש כלי פרסום... פשוט צריך להגיד ליוזר שהוא יכול לנהל קמפיינים מול גוגל
        ומטא בתשלום נוסף ישירות דרך המערכת. בלי להזכיר שם עוד דמי ניהול"*. So it says what the
        seller can DO, and that it costs extra; the percentage is disclosed on the boost screen,
        beside the budget field, where it is a number he can act on rather than a deduction from a
        price he has not agreed to yet.
        Advertising is still never offset against the subscription or the commission
        (AI_INSTRUCTIONS → Business model) — "בתשלום נוסף" is that sentence, in the seller's words. */}
    <section class="pricing-panel mt-10" aria-labelledby="ads-title">
      <h2 id="ads-title" class="text-[1.05rem] font-bold m-0">{p.adsTitle}</h2>
      <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-[0.92rem] max-w-[46rem]">{p.adsLead}</p>
      <ul role="list" class="list-none p-0 m-0 mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {adsPoints.map((line) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[0.88rem]">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 mt-[0.2rem] [color:var(--color-accent)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M4 10.5 8 14.5 16 6" />
            </svg>
            <span>{line}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initPricingTiers } from '../scripts/pricing-tiers.js';
  initPricingTiers();
</script>
